      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`/v1/messages` rejects `thinking: {\"type\": \"enabled\"}` without `budget_tokens` with a 400. Some Anthropic-compatible clients send exactly that, for example deepseek-harness, which enables thinking this way on every request, so it cannot run against SGLang with thinking on. SGLang does not enforce the budget anyway.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `budget_tokens` is optional on `thinking.type == \"enabled\"`; when present it must still be >= 1024.\n- The unit test that asserted the 400 now asserts the request is accepted with reasoning enabled.\n\n## Tests\n\n`test/registered/unit/entrypoints/anthropic/test_serving.py`: 72 passed.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:no_entry_sign: [Run #41757077284](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41757077284)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:no_entry_sign: [Run #41757077102](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41757077102)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #41757077077](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41757077077)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
